**5. Update the Bottom Action Bar**
Finally, we change the bottom buttons so that if we are in scheduling mode, it shows "Back" and "Confirm Execution".
Find your <DialogActions> block at the bottom, and update the right side of it:
```javascript
                  {/* Right Side: Action Buttons */}
                  <Stack direction="row" spacing={2} alignItems="center">
                    
                    {/* If in scheduling mode, show Back button. Otherwise show Reject */}
                    {isSchedulingMode ? (
                      <Button onClick={() => setIsSchedulingMode(false)} sx={{ fontWeight: 'bold' }}>
                        Back to Details
                      </Button>
                    ) : (
                      <Button
                        variant="contained"
                        color="error"
                        disabled={isActionDisabled || !isRemarksValid(executorRemarks) || isSubmitting}
                        onClick={() => handleSubmitAction("REJECTED")}
                        sx={{ minWidth: 120, fontWeight: 'bold' }}
                      >
                        {submittingAction === "REJECTED" ? <CircularProgress size={20} color="inherit" /> : "Reject"}
                      </Button>
                    )}

                    {/* Accept / Confirm Button */}
                    <Button
                      variant="contained"
                      color="success"
                      disabled={isActionDisabled || !isRemarksValid(executorRemarks) || isSubmitting || (scheduleOverrideType === "OVERRIDE" && !finalScheduleTime)}
                      // If NOT in scheduling mode, trigger handleInitiateAccept. If IN scheduling mode, trigger handleSubmitAction and pass the new time.
                      onClick={() => {
                        if (isSchedulingMode) {
                          // Submit with override data
                          const isOverriding = scheduleOverrideType === "OVERRIDE";
                          // You will need to briefly update your handleSubmitAction to accept the new time directly
                          handleSubmitAction("ACCEPTED", isOverriding, isOverriding ? finalScheduleTime : null); 
                        } else {
                          handleInitiateAccept();
                        }
                      }}
                      sx={{ minWidth: 120, fontWeight: 'bold' }}
                    >
                      {submittingAction === "ACCEPTED" ? <CircularProgress size={20} color="inherit" /> : (isSchedulingMode ? "Confirm & Authorize" : "Accept")}
                    </Button>
                  </Stack>

```
*(Note: Ensure your handleSubmitAction function signature accepts the extra parameters so it can pass the finalScheduleTime into your API call payload).*
